FISCAL NOTE
This bill contains an appropriation of $441,340 from the GENERAL FUND to the
Department of Parks and Cultural Resources. This appropriation is effective
immediately.
DETAIL OF APPROPRIATION
Agency #: 024 Agency Name: Department of Parks and Cultural Resources
Unit: 0215, 0216, and 0225
EXPENDITURE BY SERIES AND YEAR FY 2025 FY 2026 FY 2027
0100 Personnel/Benefit Costs $21,876 $103,909 $103,909
0200 Supportive Services Costs $12,620 $38,570 $38,570
Total Expenditure Per Year: $34,496 $142,479 $142,479
Grand Total Expenditure: $319,454
Total Appropriated to Agency: $441,340
Total Appropriated by Fund:
GENERAL FUND $441,340
In addition to the expenditures shown above, the remaining $121,886 would be
expended in FY 2028 for the remaining 36 sites. The series breakdown for FY 2028
would be $98,440 in 0100series Personnel/Benefit Costs and $23,446 in 0200series
Supportive Services Costs.
Description of appropriation:
Expenditures will include staff labor for a senior archaeologist and contract
employees to conduct fieldwork and process cultural data, required travel for
fieldwork, and equipment and software for photogrammetry.
This expenditure assumes 120 sites total with an average of three days of
fieldwork, including travel to and from the site and documentation. Required
field staff would be a senior archaeologist at $65 per hour and a technician
contract employee at $22 per hour. Each site requires data processing and entry
into the Wyoming Cultural Records Office’s WyoTrack database for long term
storage. This process entails uploading photos, scanning/digitizing field
illustrations, transcribing notes, processing geospatial data, making maps,
entering data, and other tasks as needed on a site-specific basis and assumably
will take a contract employee an estimated average of eight hours per site at $27
per hour. This also assumes the creation of a 3-dimensional model of each site
for public dissemination, which will require a photogrammetry contract employee
at $27 per hour for an estimated 16 hours per site, plus the necessary equipment
and software. The number of sites documented and modeled each fiscal year is
estimated to be eight in fiscal year 2025, 38 in fiscal year 2026, 38 in fiscal
year 2027, and 36 in fiscal year 2028.
